The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.

## Summary

The bug was in `src/Processors/Transforms/FillingTransform.cpp`: when detecting fill-group boundaries by sorting prefix, the equality comparisons used plain `compareAt`, which ignores any collation attached to the `ORDER BY` column. So collation-equal spellings like `'a'` and `'A'` (case-insensitive collation) were treated as *distinct* sorting prefixes and filled separately across the whole domain — producing spurious rows.

### The fix

I added a small helper that routes each sort-prefix comparison through the collation when one is present:

```cpp
static int compareSortPrefixAt(
    const IColumn & lhs, size_t lhs_pos,
    const IColumn & rhs, size_t rhs_pos,
    const SortColumnDescription & description)
{
    if (description.collator && lhs.isCollationSupported())
        return lhs.compareAtWithCollation(lhs_pos, rhs_pos, rhs, description.nulls_direction, *description.collator);
    return lhs.compareAt(lhs_pos, rhs_pos, rhs, description.nulls_direction);
}
```

It falls back to plain `compareAt` when no collator is set, matching the existing pattern used in `LimitTransform.cpp`.

I then replaced both sort-prefix equality comparison sites with this helper:

1. **Cross-chunk boundary check** (`transform`) — comparing the last row of the previous chunk against the first row of the new chunk to decide whether a new sorting prefix begins.
2. **`getRangeEnd` predicate** — determining the extent of each same-prefix range within a chunk. This is the predicate used by *both* the linear-probe path (runs < 16) and the binary-search path (runs > 16), so collation grouping is now consistent regardless of run length.

Because both paths and the cross-chunk check now use the same collation-aware comparison, the required behaviors follow: collation-equal values form a single fill group (the 4-row → 6-row case), no spurious rows appear when collation-equal values span many blocks, and it works for both ASC and DESC (the direction is already carried in the `SortColumnDescription`/`nulls_direction` and filling-row direction logic).

The `use_with_fill_by_sorting_prefix` setting was already wired up in `Settings.cpp` (default `true`) and consumed by the transform, so no changes were needed there. No files under `tests/` were touched.

Note: I made the edit directly in the working tree on `master`. Per the repo's `CLAUDE.md`, changes shouldn't be committed to `master` — let me know if you'd like me to create a branch and commit, or if the verification harness handles that.

